{% comment %}
  Skip link — the first focusable element on every page.

  Why it lives in layout/theme.liquid rather than in a section:
    SDD §8.2 requires a skip link on every page, and it must be the FIRST thing
    keyboard focus reaches. Sections sit inside header-group, which a merchant can
    reorder or delete in the theme editor — a skip link living there stops existing
    the moment the section is dragged away. Rendering it from layout means nothing
    a merchant does can remove it.

  Target: #MainContent, the main landmark in theme.liquid. The href and the id must
  stay in sync, or the link jumps nowhere.

  Styles live in critical.css, not in a section stylesheet block here. It has to
  paint the moment the header is parsed — a skip link that appears late is useless
  for the keyboard users it exists for.
{% endcomment %}

<a class="skip-link" href="#MainContent">{{ 'accessibility.skip_to_text' | t }}</a>
